from __future__ import annotations

NAME = "The Map and the Territory"
AMBIENCE = "Wind in Pines"

# A soothing sleep-lecture about how all our knowledge is made of maps and models, useful but never the whole world.
SECTIONS = [['You are lying down now, and there is nothing left to do.', 'Let your weight settle into the bed beneath you, slow and easy.', 'The day is behind you, and you can set it down.', 'Breathe in gently, and let the breath go without pushing it.', 'There is nowhere you need to be but here.', 'Imagine an old paper map, soft at the folds from years of handling.', 'You unfold it slowly across your lap, and it makes a quiet rustle.', 'You do not need to read it tonight, only to feel it open.', 'Each crease has been opened and closed a thousand times before.', 'Let your shoulders soften the way the paper softens at the seams.', 'Breathe out, and let the edges of the day grow gentle and blurred.', 'You are safe, and you are warm, and you can rest.'], ['A map is a quiet, lovely thing, but it is never the land itself.', 'It is paper and ink, and the land is hills, rivers, and open sky.', 'The map leaves almost everything out, and that is its gift.', 'It does not draw every blade of grass, or it could never be folded.', 'By leaving things out, it becomes small enough to carry and to read.', 'A map that showed everything would be as large as the world.', 'So the mapmaker chooses, gently, what to keep and what to let go.', 'What stays is what helps you find your way home.', 'There is a kindness in a map that knows how little it can hold.', 'It does not pretend to be the territory it points toward.', 'It only offers a path, and trusts the land to be larger.', 'Let that thought rest softly in you as you breathe.'], ['A thinker named Korzybski once said the map is not the territory.', 'He meant it gently, as a way of holding our ideas more lightly.', 'The word is not the thing, and the picture is not the place.', 'Whenever you name something, you draw a small map over the world.', 'The name tree is not the tree, with its bark and quiet roots.', 'The name river is not the cold water moving over stones.', 'Each word is a little drawing, useful and never complete.', 'And that is alright, because we were never meant to hold it all.', 'We point, and we gesture, and the world stays larger than our words.', 'You can let your words rest now, like maps folded for the night.', 'There is nothing to name in the dark, nothing to label or explain.', 'Just breathe, and let the territory be.'], ['Every theory we make is a map drawn over the wide world.', 'We picture an atom as a tiny center with specks circling around it.', 'It is a helpful drawing, but the real atom is stranger and softer than that.', 'The picture is not wrong, only small, the way all pictures are small.', 'Even a melody is a kind of map of the silence it moves through.', 'The notes mark a path, but the music is more than the marks.', 'And the face of someone you love is held as a small drawing in your mind.', 'You carry their image gently, knowing it is not the whole of them.', 'The real person is always larger, warmer, more alive than memory.', 'Your memories are maps too, soft and faded at the folds.', 'They help you find your way, and they do not need to be perfect.', 'Let them rest beside you, quiet and kind, as you breathe out.'], ['The best maps are the ones that know they are only maps.', 'They are held lightly, the way you might hold a sleepy hand.', 'A good model can be wonderfully useful and still admit it is incomplete.', 'It says, here is a path that works, and there is more I cannot show.', 'There is a deep peace in that small humility.', 'You do not have to be certain to be comforted.', 'You do not have to know everything to find your way.', 'Scientists draw their careful maps and then gently revise them.', 'Each new map is a little kinder, a little closer, never the whole.', 'And the world stays patient with all our drawings.', 'It lets us be wrong, and learn, and try again in the morning.', 'Tonight there is nothing to revise, only to rest.'], ['You do not have to hold the whole territory in your mind tonight.', 'A small, kind map is enough to rest beside.', 'The world is always larger than our drawing of it.', 'It is larger, and it is gentler, and that is a relief, not a loss.', 'There is more sky than any map could ever hold.', 'There are more rivers, more quiet valleys, more soft mornings to come.', 'You could not carry them all, and you were never asked to.', 'Let the largeness of the world be a comfort, not a weight.', 'Whatever your maps have missed, the territory keeps it safe for you.', 'It holds the parts you cannot see, and it asks nothing of you.', 'You can lay your maps down now, all of them, one by one.', 'There is room enough in the world for you to simply rest.'], ['So fold the map away now, slowly, along its soft old creases.', 'Let it close in your hands, quiet and complete.', 'You do not need it where you are going tonight.', 'The whole wide territory is already holding you, gentle and vast.', 'You are part of the land now, not the drawing of it.', 'Let your breath grow slow, and slower, like wind over far hills.', 'There is nothing more to find, nothing more to know.', 'The world is large and kind, and it has you safely.', 'Your thoughts are folding away like maps put gently to sleep.', 'Let your body grow heavy, and warm, and still.', 'You are held by something far larger than any map.', 'Rest now, and drift, and sleep.']]
